":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3.stable.flathub [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable (77dcf97d8) - Freedesktop SDK 24.08 (Flatpak runtime) - X11 - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR) - AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U with Radeon Graphics (16 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the *Bone Angle* property to rotate a bone, it does not show up in the UV editor. Is that intended?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a polygon, a skeleton and a bone as a child of the skeleton.\n2. Add a texture to the polygon.\n3. Change the *Length* and *Bone Angle* property of the bone.\n4. Attach the skeleton to the polygon.\n5. Open the UV editor of the polygon, click \"Bones\", then \"Sync Bones to Polygon\"\n6. Observe that the *Bone Angle* is not applied to the shown skeleton.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[boneangle.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18866281/boneangle.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_ur